cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EraseDub in your work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "EraseDub"
abstract: >-
  EraseDub removes burned-in subtitles from videos, translates the speech,
  and dubs the video with new voices and subtitles, running on the user's own machine.
authors:
  - name: "The EraseDub Authors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-28"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sting11k/erasedub"
keywords:
  - video-translation
  - video-translator
  - subtitle-translation
  - subtitle-removal
  - hardsub
  - hardcoded-subtitles
  - dubbing
  - ai-dubbing
  - video-dubbing
  - video-localization
  - text-to-speech
  - tts
  - speech-to-text
  - speech-recognition
  - asr
  - whisper
  - inpainting
  - video-inpainting
  - ocr
